  "comment": "Differential families run by run.sh. `request` is the Firecrawl crawl request body minus `url`: it is posted to POST /v2/crawl and the same options drive the crawlx in-process run (crawlx-differential --request). `fixture` is the gym fixture (crates/crawlx-bench/fixtures/<id>); its manifest `url_path` is the seed. `compare: cardinality` compares only the number of attempted URLs (a `limit` below the site size keeps an order-dependent subset). `expect` is the verdict the committed capture must reach with the ledger (pass: every difference is documented in divergences.toml; warn: undocumented content or counter differences; block: undocumented admission differences); `open` names the recorded residual that keeps a family at `block`. Every crawlx run uses the facade's worker canonicalization (`--trailing-slash keep`). Optional fields of the `d2` families: `host` (the name the gym is addressed by, default gym.test; the other names of the fixture are `fixture_hosts[fixture]`, which the crawlx resolver and the compose `extra_hosts` map to the gym), `seed_path` (seed below the origin instead of the manifest's `url_path`), `claim_origin` (the fixture owns the origin's robots.txt: gym-server --claim-origin, crawlx-differential --claim-origin), `aliases` (overrides `fixture_hosts`).",
